00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
there is something deeply unsettling  about an old house at night what is  beautiful if a bit worse for wear during  the day can take on a sinister cast once  the sun goes down the moan of the wind  outside the creek of the floorboards the  scraping of a branch against a window  maybe one of these sounds jolts you  awake in the dead of night eyes opening  to a room full of shadows turn twisted  and eerie in the darkness of course it's  probably nothing supernatural just an  old house settling mixed with your own  paranoia but sometimes every so often it  is something more sometimes you're not  as alone in an old house as you think  you are that's certainly the case if you  ever find yourself staying in scp-2696  also known as the haunted victorian  mansion of dark peak in 1869 wealthy and  renowned industrialist and scholar of  the occult henry percival recyth built a  stately home known as rosith hall to  house him his wife clara and any  children they might have in the future  it was constructed to provide henry with  ample space to conduct his arcane  research clara with a beautiful sitting  room and a flower garden to tend and  their future children with lots of space  to play and run around as they grew  after an uneventful year in the house  clara gave birth to two baby boys named  edgar and miles for a time the family  was happy there unfortunately this  happiness was to be short-lived as the  grim specter of death soon began to loom  over russith hall in january of 1873  clara was overcome with a sudden fever  and died in her bed this loss pushed the  already eccentric henry over the edge  and he began making strange changes to  the house's interior structure he added  hallways that led to dead ends strangely  angled floors and twisting corners  turning a once comfortable and lived-in  home into something unrecognizable in  august of that same year henry's  children edgar and miles also suddenly  passed away leaving henry alone at his  estate as he continued his descent into  madness he kept modifying the house  expanding from the mansion's library and  tower to the rest of the building's  rooms henry's days were spent  supervising the construction around the  house  refusing to let the workers carry on  without his strict oversight worried  that otherwise his vision would be  corrupted his nights were spent  sleepless as he worked away in the tower  and in the nursery on the second floor  no one was permitted to witness his work  during the night but his household staff  complained of strange sounds flashing  lights and strange whispers many were so  unsettled by these sounds and mr  rossite's erratic behavior that they  quit their jobs without notice a wise  choice given the circumstances as his  staff dwindled so too did henry russet's  already fragile grip on reality his  request for materials became more and  more imposing he demanded 200 kilograms  of ground stone from isle of angle sea  in wales and 37 meters of pipes made  from an amalgam of mercury and copper  among other unconventional materials but  rothschi still had money to burn and no  family to spend it on anymore so his  every strange request was accommodated  for a time anyway in june of 1876  exhausted and unsettled by the long  hours of work the ever increasingly  strange projects and the unusual  supernatural phenomena around the house  the remainder of ross ice workers quit  he then fired all of his household staff  with the exception of his loyal  housekeeper and resumed his work in  solitude though the specifics of just  what mr ruthsife was trying to achieve  would likely have gone to the grave with  him some of his diary entries were  recovered from the house and they  provide a peek into his motives and  nature of the mansion's anomalous  activity after the death of his wife and  children he became obsessed with the  concept of the mind-made body the notion  that having a memory so strong that if  given the proper energetic conditions it  could take on corporeal form his theory  was if a memory is engraved permanently  in the mind it could then take on a  permanent physical and energetic  manifestation he began to experiment  with this concept determined to bring  back a form of his wife and children by  any means necessary a noble pursuit that  paved the way for madness it is during  this process that he began to remodel  the house in order to provide the ideal  energetic conditions for his memories to  be made material eventually his notes  devolved into nonsense and the pages  were covered with geometric equations  and blood his final entry reads the  children still speak in her voice i fear  i might be going mad it is true that he  might have been losing his grip on  sanity towards the end of his  experiments but his work undeniably  filled the house with something it was  not long before reports of strange  sights and sounds around the russith  home reached the ears of those trained  to investigate such matters the house  and its anomalous nature were initially  discovered by jintinder jaishankar an  occultist and investigator employed by  the royal foundation for the secure  containment of the paranormal or rfscp  he wrote the first official report on  the house in 1876  after investigating multiple rumors of  ghostly sightings around the house he  and his team a married pair of ghost  hunters named the bartons arrived at the  rossite home with a sense of  apprehension they were ushered through  the door by a housekeeper who made the  eerie promise that henry russith would  be with them shortly when the master of  the house came to greet them the  investigative team was shocked by his  appearance he was gaunt almost skeletal  with a dark set eyes bleary from  entirely too long without sleep he  looked as if he had aged a hundred years  in the few years since his wife's death  the team stayed the night in the house  experiencing a restless and nightmare  adult sleep until 2 30 am when the  investigative work was to begin they  descended down to the main hall of the  house where a large black door was all  that stood between them and the unknown  it opened with a bone-deep groan as if  to warn them not to enter but still they  stepped inside once they crossed the  threshold they were greeted with odd  angles a garish array of colors and  materials and bewilderingly high  ceilings all to mr ross scythe's very  demanding specifications of course he  spared no expense in making his  nonsensical nightmare house an  unsettling reality the bartons presented  dowsing rods which they used to measure  spiritual activity in the room at first  nothing happened but soon the dowsing  rods began to spark viciously and a  sudden gust of wind blew out all the  candles in the room there was nothing  but darkness and the sudden sense of a  heavy presence among them the bartons  dropped to the floor with mrs barton  leaking blood from her mouth and dr  barton convulsing violently the presence  grew stronger and though it did not  speak it was unmistakable who it was it  was the deceased clara rossith  jaishankar fled the manor dragging his  unconscious companions out as fast as he  could once safely away from the mansion  he immediately contacted the rfs cp well  as quickly as one can when communicating  by telegram a second team was sent to  investigate the house in the following  days but when they arrived henry russith  could not be found there was no sign of  a struggle no body he simply  vanished he was never seen again  the scp foundation has an official  record of two separate incorporeal  entities that dwell within the walls of  scp-2696  the first  scp-2696-1 appears to be the ghost or  memory energetic signature whatever you  wish to call it of clara rossais the  apparition is the one that jintinder  jaikansha and the bartons encountered  she is translucent and intangible and  most frequently appears in the form of  clara as a young mother at the pinnacle  of her good health she has also  occasionally taken on several inhuman  forms including a wilting plumeria bush  and a disturbing column of bone muscle  and flesh exposure to the clara entity  has a pronounced negative effect on  anyone who comes near her people that  come within several feet of  scp-2696 have reported mild visual and  auditory hallucinations such as creeping  shadows and whispering voices chanting  in foreign languages there have also  been reports of amnesia fainting  seizures bleeding from the nose mouth  and ears and in the most severe cases  disassociative episodes that result in  complete losses of identity many of  these physical side effects are thought  to be the result of the massive amounts  of radiation that have been measured  being given off by the entity the second  entity in the house known as scp-2696-2  is actually two entities that always  seem to come as a pair known as 2a and  2b these are the skeletons of miles and  edgar rossith the deceased children of  clara and henry they're located inside  of the nursery which is inaccessible to  outsiders with the door that seems able  to seal itself shut at will and keep  researchers out the two skeletons are  largely inactive remaining on the floor  of the nursery in the fetal position at  nearly all times they only become active  during periods of extreme activity from  the clara entity when clara is  especially active and attempting to  leave her usual domain in the house's  tower the skeletons have been reported  to wrestle and play with each other  dance around the room or stand at the  door to the nursery appearing to be  waiting for something one notable  occasion though on june 12 1990 both  instances of  scp-2696-2 were able to actually leave  the nursery and travel elsewhere in the  house a series of massive lightning  strikes raised the energy levels in the  house and clara's radiation levels  suddenly spiked significantly surge  protectors placed in the house failed  and clara became more active than usual  transforming into a swirling dark mass  that emitted an ear splitting shriek the  front door of the mansion slammed itself  shut and refused to open trapping the  research team who were present at the  time they were only able to exit after  scp-2696-2a  and 2b were spotted leaving the nursery  hand in hand they approached clara and  opened their arms to her pacified  perhaps by some distant echo of a  mother's love the entity quieted and the  foundation team was finally able to  leave it is still unknown how 2a and 2b  were able to leave the nursery but there  have not been any incidences of this  level since currently the dark peak  mansion remains standing and is largely  untouched from how its creator left it  the scp foundation maintains a strict  perimeter of one square kilometer around  the house and no civilians are permitted  to cross it not only is the building  restricted for civilians most scp  personnel are also forbidden from  entering the house some of the only ones  who are allowed inside are a special  class of scp foundation personnel  experimental containment research group  or ecrg and mtf theta 77 nicknamed who  you gonna call given what was learned in  the 1990 activation event it is apparent  that the containment procedures have a  rate of failure that does not adequately  contain  scp-2696-1 and according to the  containment file there is a 47 chance of  clara breaching containment completely  by 2030. catherine stedman once wrote  houses aren't haunted people are henry  russith was so haunted by the loss of  his beloved wife and children that he  could not stand to live in his big empty  house all alone henry russeth may be  long gone but his attempts to grasp at  that which was long gone before him have  forever changed the house he built his  grief his pain his energy filled the  house with echoes of his loved ones and  as pain often does when left untreated  it began to fester and turn foul dr  henry russeth was a deeply haunted man  and now his haunted house is all that  remains of him now go check out  scp-1730 what happened to site 13 the  full story compilation and  scp-1337 the hitchhiker for more  anomalies that'll chill you to the bone

